---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/hazard.css';
import HazardRuleTester from '../../components/HazardRuleTester.vue';
---
<BaseLayout title="Hazard Detector" description="Real-time hazard detection for e-scooters with YOLOv8 and MobileSAM. A four-person IEEE Quarterly Project; I built the road-path segmentation." image="/hazard-detector/assets/poster.jpg">
<div class="wrap case-study">
  <header class="top">
    <a class="label" href="/projects/">← All projects</a>
    <nav aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#rule-sec">Alert rule</a>
      <a href="#path">Path detection</a>
      <a href="#pipeline">Pipeline</a>
      <a href="#team">Team</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <span class="label">IEEE Quarterly Project · Spring 2026 · team of 4</span>
      <h1>Hazard Detector</h1>
      <p class="lede">A camera on an e-scooter streams video into a computer-vision pipeline that <strong>spots potholes, rocks, curbs, stairs, speed bumps, people and vehicles, and beeps only when one is actually in the rider's path</strong>. I built the part that finds the path: a MobileSAM model that outlines the road surface ahead.</p>
      <div class="links">
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/kdbell4/hazard-detector">Source on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://devpost.com/software/hazard-detection-system">Devpost demo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="phone">
      <video id="demo" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster="assets/poster.jpg" aria-label="Night ride along a campus bike path with the detected road surface shaded green and detections boxed">
        <source src="assets/demo.webm" type="video/webm">
        <source src="assets/demo.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
      <figcaption class="caption">Our test ride, re-run through MobileSAM and the base YOLO model. Green is the road surface the path step finds. The people later in the clip are detected but stay quiet: they are too small and too far up the frame to be a threat.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="specs">
    <div><span class="label">My role</span><span class="v">Path segmentation</span></div>
    <div><span class="label">Detection</span><span class="v">YOLOv8n + 5 custom</span></div>
    <div><span class="label">Segmentation</span><span class="v">MobileSAM</span></div>
    <div><span class="label">App</span><span class="v">FastAPI dashboard</span></div>
  </div>

  <section id="rule-sec">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">The alert rule</span>
      <h2>Three checks before it beeps</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="prose">A detector that beeps at every car in frame is useless, because most of them are parked or far away. An object only counts as a hazard when it is <b>big enough to be close</b>, <b>sitting on the road ahead</b>, and <b>low in the frame</b>. Drag the box around this frame from our test ride, or resize it from the corner, to see the rule decide.</p>
    <HazardRuleTester client:visible />
  </section>

  <section id="path">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">My part · path detection</span>
      <h2>Finding the road with three seed points</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="two">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Before path detection, the "in path" check was a fixed strip down the middle of the frame. That breaks on curves and whenever the camera tilts, which happens constantly on a scooter.</p>
        <p>Segment Anything models take prompts: give them a point and they return the mask of the object under it. The pixels just in front of the front wheel are almost always road, so I seed MobileSAM with three points along the bottom edge, at 2/5, 1/2 and 3/5 of the width. Of the masks it returns, I keep the largest one and turn it into a polygon. The rest of the app can then test any point against it with <code>cv2.pointPolygonTest</code>.</p>
        <p>Segmentation is the slowest model in the pipeline, so it runs on every fifth inference frame and the polygon is reused in between. The road ahead barely changes in a sixth of a second.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="min-width:0">
        <p class="file">webapp/engine.py · _update_path_polygon</p>
<pre>points = [[2 * w // 5, h],      <span class="c"># left of the wheel</span>
          [w // 2,     h],      <span class="c"># straight ahead</span>
          [3 * w // 5, h]]      <span class="c"># right of the wheel</span>
results = self._sam.predict(frame, conf=0.25,
                            points=points, verbose=False)
<span class="k">if</span> results[0].masks <span class="k">and</span> results[0].masks.xy:
    <span class="h">self._path_polygon = max(results[0].masks.xy,
                             key=cv2.contourArea)</span></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="two">
      <div class="prose">
        <h3 style="margin-bottom:10px">How it developed</h3>
        <p>I prototyped on a still image first, then on recorded ride video, then reduced the output to the single polygon the hazard logic needs before merging it into the team repo.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="timeline">
        <li><time>Apr 28</time><span>Segmented a single road image with SAM</span></li>
        <li><time>Apr 29</time><span>Ran it on ride video, prompted by one point</span></li>
        <li><time>May 4</time><span>Switched to three seed points and kept only the largest mask as a polygon</span></li>
        <li><time>May 13</time><span>Refactored and merged into the team repo</span></li>
        <li><time>May 26</time><span>Added SAM 2.1 tiny weights to the main repo to try as a replacement</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="pipeline">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">Pipeline</span>
      <h2>From camera frame to beep</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flow">
      <div><span class="n">Capture thread</span><h3>Camera</h3><p>Webcam or video file, one-frame buffer so inference always sees the newest frame.</p><span class="rate">full frame rate</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">Ultralytics YOLO</span><h3>Detection</h3><p>YOLOv8n filtered to people, vehicles and animals, plus five custom-trained hazard models.</p><span class="rate">base every frame, custom every 3rd</span></div>
      <div class="mine"><span class="n">MobileSAM · my part</span><h3>Road path</h3><p>Largest mask from three bottom-edge seed points, kept as a polygon.</p><span class="rate">every 5th frame</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">Hazard logic</span><h3>Alert rule</h3><p>Close enough, in the path, and low in frame. Per-label cooldown so one pothole beeps once.</p><span class="rate">per detection</span></div>
      <div><span class="n">FastAPI</span><h3>Alert + dashboard</h3><p>Audio alert, CSV log, and a browser dashboard with the live feed and model toggles.</p><span class="rate">MJPEG stream</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption prose">Capture and inference run on separate threads, so the video stays smooth while the boxes update as fast as the hardware allows. The engine picks Apple MPS, CUDA or CPU automatically.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="team">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">Team</span>
      <h2>Who built what</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="me"><span class="role">Me · path detection</span><h3>Kenny</h3><p>MobileSAM road segmentation, so alerts only fire for objects in the scooter's path. Also set up the repo and the first YOLO + OpenCV demo.</p></div>
      <div><span class="role">Hazard logic + integration</span><h3>Toby</h3><p>The rule that decides when an object is a threat, and the web app that combines everyone's work.</p></div>
      <div><span class="role">Custom models</span><h3>Ashwin</h3><p>Trained the pothole, rock, stair, curb and speed-bump models from Roboflow datasets and collected data.</p></div>
      <div><span class="role">Alerts</span><h3>Katherine</h3><p>Audio playback, the cooldown that stops constant beeping, and timestamped CSV logging.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="label">Tools</span>
      <h2>Stack</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="stack"><span>Python</span><span>Ultralytics YOLOv8</span><span>MobileSAM</span><span>OpenCV</span><span>PyTorch (MPS / CUDA)</span><span>FastAPI</span><span>pygame</span><span>Roboflow</span></div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span>Hazard Detector</span>
    <a class="mono" href="https://github.com/kdbell4/hazard-detector">kdbell4/hazard-detector</a>
  </footer>
</div>
<script>
  const video = document.getElementById('demo');
  if (video && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
    video.removeAttribute('autoplay');
    video.pause();
    video.controls = true;
  }
</script>
</BaseLayout>
